IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bea-cheques`

-- Bills of Exchange Act 1949, ss 3, 8(1), 9(2), 14, 22(3), 24, 26, 29, 48-50, 64, 73-76, 79, 81, 82, 99 and 101 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_bills-of-exchange-act-1949.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `Fixtures`

`a personal cheque to a named payee` MEANS Instrument WITH
    `an order rather than a promise` IS TRUE
    `in writing` IS TRUE
    `signed by the drawer` IS TRUE
    `drawn on a banker` IS TRUE
    `payable on demand` IS TRUE
    `payable at a fixed or determinable future time` IS FALSE
    `payable on a contingency` IS FALSE
    `for a sum certain in money` IS TRUE
    `to a specified person or to bearer` IS TRUE
    `payable only out of a particular fund` IS FALSE
    `orders some act besides paying money` IS FALSE
    `names the account to be debited` IS FALSE
    `undated` IS FALSE
    `post-dated` IS FALSE

